This repository holds two different things, under two different licences.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The artwork, in art/ — CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

To the extent possible under law, KyronLabs and the contributors named in
catalogue.json have waived all copyright and related or neighbouring rights
to the images in art/.

You may use them for anything, including commercially, without permission,
payment or attribution.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Why CC0 and not something with attribution: this artwork exists so that
somebody can publish a lens with it, and a published lens is then copied,
remixed, and served from a CDN to people who will never read this file. A
licence with an attribution requirement would make every one of those an
obligation nobody is tracking, on people who did not choose it. Each entry
in catalogue.json still names its author, because credit is worth giving
even where it is not owed.

